#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute noisy, unmitigated expectation values {#compute-noisy-unmitigated-"
"expectation-values}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A ``QuantumProgram`` contains a quantum circuit and a samplex in a format "
"suitable for the [Executor primitive](/guides/get-started-with-executor). "
"`MitigationTask.prepare` builds a ``QuantumProgram`` from the circuit, the "
"observables, and the parameter values, and boxes the circuit with the given "
"boxing options.Set the ``measure_annotations`` boxing option to "
"``\"change_basis\"``, which rotates the measurements into the required "
"bases, and add ``add_tags: \"unique_box\"`` so the simulator can map a noise"
" model onto the boxes of the circuit. The program is Pauli-twirled by "
"default, which on hardware turns coherent noise into the Pauli noise that "
"the mitigation methods assume. `num_randomizations` sets how many twirled "
"instances of each circuit are sampled, and `shots_per_randomization` sets "
"how many shots each instance receives, so their product is the shot budget "
"per circuit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A user with QPU access would execute the program with an `Executor` built "
"from a backend of the `QiskitRuntimeService`. Here you will pass an "
"`AerSimulator` to the `Executor`, which runs the program locally, and use "
"its `layer_noise_model` simulator option to inject a random Pauli-Lindblad "
"noise model on every layer of entangling gates, generated with "
"`random_pauli_lindblad_noise` from `qiskit-mitigation` with an error per "
"layered gate (EPLG) of ``0.003``, typical of current Heron QPUs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning/extracted-"
"outputs/feaad655-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Learn the noise of the entangling layers with `qiskit-noise-learning` "
"{#learn-the-noise-of-the-entangling-layers-with-qiskit-noise-learning}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling "
"gates in the circuit. We assume a Markovian noise model, and therefore only "
"the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned, "
"because the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel "
"of a given entangling layer. The more accurate the learned noise model is, "
"the more accurate the amplification will be.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We use `qiskit-noise-learning` for learning the noise. The learner repeats "
"each layer `fragment_depths` times in its learning circuits, twirls each "
"circuit `num_randomizations` times, and fits the decay of the measured "
"fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. The following code draws the learned "
"noise model, with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of"
" its weight-1 X, Y, and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge "
"shows the learned weight-2 rates; a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs"
" on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning/extracted-"
"outputs/597571c1-9c50-4ed0-a18d-71a5a5342413-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare a ZNE program with probabilistic error amplification and sample "
"circuits of varying noise scales {#prepare-a-zne-program-with-probabilistic-"
"error-amplification-and-sample-circuits-of-varying-noise-scales}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here you will prepare a ZNE program containing circuits of increasing noise "
"scales. With PEA, each noise factor represents the multiple of the learned "
"noise the circuit experiences: a noise factor of ``2.0`` injects one "
"additional copy of each layer's learned noise channel after that layer, on "
"top of the noise the layer already has. Because PEA scales the learned noise"
" rates directly rather than repeating gates, any noise factor is possible, "
"including non-integer ones, and the circuit itself is not modified: the "
"program items share one template circuit and differ only in the noise "
"injected by the samplex. The injected noise is sampled once per "
"randomization, so the statistical error of PEA is controlled by the number "
"of randomizations rather than the shots per randomization; we therefore use "
"many randomizations with a few shots each, keeping the total number of shots"
" the same as for the unmitigated program. It is important to not use too few"
" randomizations, as otherwise you might encounter sampling bias in the noise"
" injection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The total sampling overhead scales linearly with the number of noise "
"factors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, run the program on the noisy simulator. Its results feed the "
"extrapolation in the next step.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extrapolate to the zero-noise limit {#extrapolate-to-the-zero-noise-limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that you have data for each noise scale, you can fit a function to the "
"data and extrapolate back to the zero-noise value to estimate an expectation"
" value of the noise-free observable. Under Pauli noise an observable decays "
"exponentially with the noise factor, so you will choose the exponential "
"extrapolator as your first choice, and fall back to the linear one if the "
"exponential fit fails. To visualize the extrapolation, plot the site-"
"averaged magnetization calculated at each noise factor, the exponential fit,"
" and the site average of the extrapolated expectation values at the zero-"
"noise point. We see the fit slightly undershoots for this particular "
"observable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning/extracted-"
"outputs/18f5c3d3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

